On Sun, Feb 12, 2012 at 11:44 AM, Remo Dentato <rdentato@gmail.com> wrote:

> On Sun, Feb 12, 2012 at 6:23 PM, Jonathan Jones <eyeonus@gmail.com> wrote=
:
> > How do you type an accented character on a U.S. keyboard? We don't have=
 a
> > compose key, unless we're running Linux and set, say, caps-lock to it..=
..
>
> Using   Left Alt  + code (on numeric pad)  should work (it does on my
> WIndows 7 box)
>
> 133     =E0
> 138     =E8
> 141     =EC
> 149     =F2
> 151     =F9
>
> I used this long time ago, when the Italian keyboards didn't have the
> characters "{`}" and I was programming in C (btw, the Italian keyboard
> doesn't have the bactick still Alt+96).
>
> Should everything else fail, the charmap.exe utility (in the
> Accessories folder) will let you copy the accented characters in the
> clipboard (and you'll have to paste them where you need them).
>

Oh, I know about the charmap and the alt thing. However, their is a lot
more effort involved in both those methods then merely using Capital
letters, and in general humans are very lazy. O requires two keystrokes. =
=F2
requires at least 4 using the ALT+n method as well as requiring one to
memorize it's number, and charmap is so inefficient it's not worth talking
about. Using a compose key is really the only way that's viable competition
to using capitals: <compose>,o,` is only one more keystroke than <shift>+o,
and doesn't require much more in the way of memorization.


> Considering how infrequently accented characters are used in Lojban, I
> would consider this a little hindrance compared to having to throw
> capital letters in the middle of a lojban word.
>
> remod


Personally, I'm not really concerned with punctuation marking method. I'll
agree that using accents are more appealing visually, but I'm in agreement
with .xorxes. in that the pronunciation of a word does not change the
word-- .*ai*onys., .a*io*nys., .*aio*nys., etc. are all the same word: my
name. (Apologies to those which have a mail client that interprets
underlining by displaying it as ._ai_onys.)

--=20
